-- title:
--   Reduction inputs modulo ℓ exist when ℓ∤ N
-- statement:
--   Let $N$ be a nonzero natural number and $\ell$ a prime with $\ell\nmid N$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}=$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` which lies over $\ell$ in the sense of [`ValuationSubring.LiesOverPrime`](def/FLTPrelim_Ramification.html#L16), that is, the image of $\ell$ in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is a nonunit of $A$ (equivalently, $\ell$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$). The conclusion is [`ModularCurve.ReductionInputsModL A N`](def/ModularCurve_ReductionModL.html#L184), which by definition is [`ModularCurve.ReductionInputsAlong A (IsLocalRing.residue A) N`](def/ModularCurve_ReductionModL.html#L40), taken along the residue map $\pi\colon A\to k_A$ of the local ring $A$: there exists a map $r$ on places, from the places of the modular function field of level $N$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ to the places of its counterpart over the residue field $k_A$, such that the predicate [`ModularCurve.IsPlaceReductionAlong A (IsLocalRing.residue A) N r`](def/ModularCurve_ReductionModL.html#L18) holds for $r$, and such that the predicate [`ModularCurve.PrincipalGeneratedByIntegral A (IsLocalRing.residue A) N`](def/ModularCurve_ReductionModL.html#L36) holds; the former expresses that $r$ reduces places compatibly with the coefficientwise reduction of Laurent series along $\pi$, the latter that principal divisors are generated by divisors of elements integral for $A$.
--
--   This is the good-reduction statement for the modular curve of level $N$ at a prime $\ell$ not dividing $N$, packaged in Deuring's language of reduction of an algebraic function field along a place of its constant field: it supplies the place-reduction map $r$ and the generation property that together form the input data for working with the curve modulo $\ell$. It is the entry point for the many downstream results on newforms, Tate modules and Frobenius and inertia at $\ell$ that invoke [`ModularCurve.ReductionInputsModL`](def/ModularCurve_ReductionModL.html#L184).
-- source:
